================================================================================
## Fix the 13 bugs pinned by the 0.9.0 tests
================================================================================

Context:
The previous section pinned 13 real bugs with strict xfail markers. Each is
fixed at its root cause and its marker removed. Three of them came from the
0.9.0 god-class extraction (commit 817b0a9e), which dropped imports and a class
constant that the extracted code still referenced; a scan of every class that
commit produced found no other dangling `self.<name>` / module-alias lookups.

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   Restored the `DatabricksClient`, `is_databricks_app`, `PERMISSIONS_APPS_PATH`
   and `is_neo4j_password_from_secret` imports. The extracted settings classes
   resolve them through the `_ss` module alias, so Neo4j basic-auth status and
   the graph-engine health check raised AttributeError.
2. src/back/objects/domain/GraphEngineSettings.py
   Duplicate Neo4j connection names are checked on the raw submitted list;
   `list_neo4j_connections` de-duplicates names, so the guard never fired.
3. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/LakebaseRegistryAnalytics.py
   Restored `_GRAPH_ANALYTICS_RUNS_CAP = 100`; recording a graph analytics run
   raised AttributeError instead of pruning history.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinMapping.py
   New-entity `uri_template` ended in `}}` (`.../Customer/{cid}}`).
5. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/QualitySqlBuilder.py
   An unknown `value_check_type` returns None (check skipped) instead of SQL
   with no filter that flagged every value; startsWith/endsWith/contains escape
   LIKE wildcards in the check value.
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/SqlQualityChecks.py
   SWRL progress uses an explicit `offset=len(shapes)`; `total - len(swrl)`
   assumed SWRL ran last, so progress jumped back when decision tables or
   aggregate rules followed.
7. src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py, src/back/core/helpers/__init__.py
   New `sql_like_escape` + `LIKE_ESCAPE` (`ESCAPE '!'`): makes `%`/`_` literal
   in LIKE patterns on both Spark and Postgres, which disagree on backslashes.
8. src/back/core/graphdb/entity_search.py, src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBBackend.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/GraphFind.py
   Entity search, typed lookup, find-subjects and triples/find seeds escape
   LIKE wildcards in user search values and entity type names (`a_b` no longer
   matches `axb`). Exact matches are unchanged.
9. src/back/objects/ontology/OntologyOwl.py
   `_turtle_to_camel` only changes each word's first letter; `capitalize()` /
   `lower()` flattened existing camelCase (`:OrderLine` → `:Orderline`) and undid
   the snake_case fix (`:first_name` → `:firstname`) in LLM-generated OWL.
10. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyParser.py
    Header-less OWL gets an empty label instead of "Unknown Ontology", so the
    import falls back to the domain name.
11. src/back/core/w3c/rdfs/RDFSParser.py
    RDFS base URI is the namespace most declared classes/properties use; the
    first bound prefix was an rdflib default (e.g. `brick`). Bound prefixes are
    only a fallback when some subject actually uses them.
12. src/back/core/w3c/shacl/SHACLParser.py
    Imported shape ids end with a content hash instead of a random suffix, so
    re-importing the same SHACL file replaces shapes instead of duplicating them.
13. Tests
    - tests/units/settings/test_v090_settings_facade.py: new guard test — every
      `_ss.<name>` read by the extracted settings classes must exist.
    - Removed the strict xfail markers from all fixed tests; the health test now
      patches `_ss.DatabricksClient`; dropped the redundant duplicate-guard test.
    - tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_dq_sql_builder.py,
      tests/units/graphdb/test_v090_graph_access_filter.py: assert the escaped
      pattern positively; added `!` doubling and exact-match tests.
    - tests/units/graphdb/test_entity_search_sql.py,
      tests/units/graphdb/test_graphdb_adjacency_contract.py: expected SQL now
      carries `ESCAPE '!'`.

